sp("V04-C-005", "History and politics",
   "Printing, driven by commercial need, pushed books into vernacular languages and divided Europe into separate reading publics.",
   "Easy",
   ["Before the printing press spread across Europe in the late fifteenth century, most serious writing was in Latin, the shared language of scholars, clergy and lawyers.",
    "Manuscripts were copied by hand for small audiences, and a scholar in one country could read a scholar in another precisely because both used the same learned tongue.",
    "Printers, however, were people of business, and they needed to sell many copies of each book to recover the cost of paper, type and labour.",
    "Over the following centuries vernacular books multiplied, and the spellings chosen by printing houses gradually hardened into national standards.",
    "Latin did not vanish, but it slowly retreated into the universities and the church while the wider conversation of print moved elsewhere.",
    "The machine that might have bound learned Europe more tightly together thus helped to divide it into separate reading publics, each with its own language of print."],
   "That commercial pressure pushed them towards the languages that ordinary readers actually spoke.",
   [1, 3, 4, 6],
   "The missing sentence begins 'That commercial pressure', which refers back to the printers' need to 'sell many copies of each book' in the third sentence, and it explains why the vernacular books of the next sentence multiplied. It belongs at gap (2).",
   {1: "At gap (1) nothing commercial has yet been mentioned; the paragraph is still describing Latin and hand-copied manuscripts.",
    4: "At gap (3) vernacular books have already multiplied and standards formed, so the cause would arrive after its effect, far from the printers' need it refers to.",
    6: "At gap (4) the paragraph has drawn its conclusion with 'thus', and the reference to commercial pressure would be stranded at the end."},
   "Choosing gap (3) because the sentence about Latin retreating seems to need a cause, overlooking that 'That commercial pressure' must sit right after the printers' need to sell.",
   "V04C-printing-vernacular-languages",
   "A direct backward reference to the printers' commercial need fixes the gap.",
   cognitive="Understanding")

