sp("V04-C-009", "Cities and geography",
   "Street vendors serve real needs, so the question is how to accommodate them on the pavement, not whether to remove them.",
   "Easy",
   ["City authorities often regard street vendors as an obstacle, a clutter of carts and stalls that narrows the pavement and slows the movement of pedestrians.",
    "Clearing them away is therefore presented as a simple improvement, a return of public space to the public.",
    "Yet vendors are themselves part of that public, and many of the people they serve are workers with neither the time nor the money for a shop or a restaurant.",
    "A tea stall outside a bus depot or a fruit cart near a hospital meets a need that no formal business has chosen to meet at that spot.",
    "Vendors also keep a street watched and occupied after offices close, which can make it feel safer for those walking home late.",
    "The means of doing so need not be elaborate: marked zones, fixed hours and modest licence fees have all been tried in different places, and none of them requires treating vendors as trespassers."],
   "The real question for a city, then, is not whether vendors belong on its pavements but how to make room for them without blocking the way.",
   [1, 3, 5, 6],
   "The missing sentence draws a conclusion ('then') from the case for vendors: the needs they meet and the safety they bring. It also asks 'how to make room for them', and the last sentence answers that question: 'The means of doing so' refers to making room, and the zones, hours and fees are those means. It must come after the safety point and before the list of methods, at gap (3).",
   {1: "At gap (1) the paragraph has only stated the authorities' view; there is no case for vendors yet from which 'then' could draw a conclusion.",
    3: "At gap (2) the paragraph has only just begun its reply with 'Yet'; concluding here would cut off the tea stall example and the safety point that the conclusion rests on.",
    6: "At gap (4) the ways of making room have already been listed, and 'The means of doing so' in the last sentence would have nothing to refer to, since making room would not yet have been mentioned."},
   "Choosing gap (4) because a sentence with 'then' looks like a natural ending, without noticing that 'The means of doing so' in the last sentence needs this sentence just before it.",
   "V04C-street-vendors-pavements",
   "A concluding 'then' plus a question answered in the next sentence make the position clear once both links are read.",
   cognitive="Understanding")

