sp("V04-C-019", "Psychology",
   "Effort falls in groups mainly because individual contributions become invisible, so the remedy is to make them visible.",
   "Medium",
   ["When people work together on a shared task, the total effort of the group is often less than the sum of what each member would produce alone.",
    "Part of the shortfall is simply a matter of coordination, since people pulling on the same rope rarely pull at exactly the same moment.",
    "But a larger part seems to come from a quieter change in motivation.",
    "When individual contributions cannot be seen, each member can ease off a little without being noticed, and many do.",
    "Appeals to try harder therefore tend to fail, because each member assumes that the appeal is addressed to someone else.",
    "What works better is to make contributions visible, or to give each person a part of the task that is recognisably their own.",
    "Groups, in short, do not make people lazy so much as they make laziness invisible, and the remedy is to restore visibility."],
   "This hidden slackening is rarely a conscious decision to shirk, and most people who do it would sincerely deny that they had.",
   [1, 2, 4, 6],
   "'This hidden slackening' refers to members easing off 'without being noticed' in the fourth sentence. The missing sentence adds that they do not realise it, which is why, as the next sentence says, appeals to try harder 'therefore' fail: each member sincerely thinks the appeal is meant for someone else. It belongs at gap (3).",
   {1: "At gap (1) only the overall shortfall has been mentioned; no slackening, hidden or otherwise, has yet been described.",
    2: "At gap (2) the paragraph has described a problem of timing on the rope, which is neither hidden nor a slackening, and the sentence would also separate 'Part of the shortfall' from 'But a larger part', which answers it.",
    6: "At gap (4) the remedy has already been given, and the sentence would come between the remedy and the summing up, far from the easing off it refers to."},
   "Choosing gap (2) because the rope example seems to describe a loss of effort, overlooking that coordination is not slackening and that 'But a larger part' must follow 'Part of the shortfall'.",
   "V04C-social-loafing",
   "The backward reference is clear only once the solver sees that coordination losses are not slackening; the forward link to 'therefore' completes the fit.")

